Package: gh0st-wifi
Version: @WIFI_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: CPZeroOS <15324879+therezor@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Depends: udev, systemd
Description: Wi-Fi for Gh0st OS: the built-in chip's boot retry, USB firmware
 The built-in BCM43439 can fail its firmware download at boot ("Downloaded
 RAM image is corrupted"), and brcmfmac then lets the chip go. A udev rule
 binds it again, at most twice a boot.
 .
 Also firmware for USB Wi-Fi adapters whose drivers do monitor mode:
 Atheros AR9271 and AR7010, the Ralink RT2870 family (RT3070, RT5370 and
 kin), MediaTek MT7601U, MT7610U, MT7612U and MT7921AU, Realtek RTL8812AU,
 RTL8811AU, RTL8821AU, RTL8814AU, RTL8822BU, RTL8811CU, RTL8821CU,
 RTL8822CU and RTL8723DU. The files come from Raspberry Pi's
 firmware-atheros, firmware-mediatek and firmware-realtek.
